==English==

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# The property of an [[electric circuit]] by which a [[voltage]] is [[induce]]d in it by a changing [[magnetic field]].
#:''The power cable itself has enough '''inductance''' to disrupt the digital signal of the video output cable, due to poor shielding.''
# The [[quantity]] of the resulting electromagnetic flux divided by the current that produces it, measured in [[henry|henries]] (SI symbol: '''H'''.)
#:''What is the '''inductance''' of that power supply's main inductor?''

